# Taskbar Unresponsive
## Incident:
Customer reports that their windows taskbar is missing since logging into their computer this morning. They have checked their display wasn’t accidentally in full screen mode.
## Troubleshooting Steps:
- Troubleshooting based on Windows 11
- If the user has accidentally enabled the “automatically hide taskbar” setting. To get to this without the taskbar: Windows key + I to open the settings > Personalisation in the right hand menu > Select the downwards arrow next to “Taskbar Behaviours". Disable the “automatically hide taskbar option”.
- If the taskbar has stopped functioning, follow the steps below.
## Cause Determined:
Windows Explorer was unresponsive.
## Action Plan:
1. Press ctrl + shift+ esc keys to open the task manager
2. Find the “Windows Explorer” task in the “Processes” list
3. Right click on “Windows Explorer” and select “Restart”
4. If the Taskbar does not reappear, Press Ctrl + Alt + Dlt, press the power button in the bottom right corner and select “Restart”.
## Customer Response:
The customer can access the taskbar again after restarting their computer.
